{
  "id": "10-guard-the-temple",
  "title": "Guard What God Entrusted",
  "tenet": "Honor God in body and mind",
  "durationMs": 75120,
  "audioAsset": "kingdom/10-guard-the-temple.mp3",
  "transcriptAsset": "assets/kingdom/10-guard-the-temple.json",
  "text": "What do you protect when nobody else can see the cost?\n\nA young man kept a small lamp beside the notebook where he wrote his hopes. Each night he meant to pray and plan the next day. Instead he stayed awake chasing a pleasure that left him restless. One morning the glass was dark with soot, and he could scarcely read the page. His sister helped him clean it. The lamp was not worthless; its light had been obscured. He moved it, made room for sleep, and asked a trusted friend to help him keep the new rhythm.\n\nWe can wrong a neighbor. When we sin against ourselves, we also sin against God, who entrusted this life to us. Scripture calls the body a temple of the Holy Spirit. Flee sexual immorality and anything that treats another person as an object. Resist drunkenness and chronic laziness when they become patterns that steal attention from love and work. If weariness, illness, or dependence is involved, seek care rather than hiding in shame. Sin does not erase your worth or place you beyond God's mercy. It can cloud the witness and freedom God wants to grow in you. Ask daily for grace to guard your body and purify your mind. Put one goal you prayed for before your eyes, and make one choice that serves it today.",
